# HomerScribe .gitignore
#
# What is here belongs in the repository. What is listed below does not: it is
# either large, regenerable, or somebody's working material.

# ---- build products --------------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is made by buildHomerScribe.cmd from what IS in the
# repository, so keeping them would be storing the output alongside the input.
*.exe
*.zip
Version.cs

# ---- tools fetched at build time -------------------------------------------
# Hundreds of megabytes, and downloaded or copied by the build.
ffmpeg.exe
ffprobe.exe
ffplay.exe
yt-dlp.exe
youtube-dl.exe

# ---- media -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Films and recordings being worked on. Never part of the program, and the
# reason a push was once rejected.
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mov
*.webm
*.mpg
*.mpeg
*.wmv
*.flv
*.ts
*.m2ts
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac

# ---- what a run produces ---------------------------------------------------
work/
described.*
transcribed.*
scribed.*
*.log

# ---- maintainer's own material ---------------------------------------------
# Announcement drafts, notes and lists: written for use elsewhere and no part
# of the source. Announce.md and Announce.htm are NOT here -- they ship with
# the program and are named in HomerScribe_setup.iss.
Facebook.*
LinkedIn.*
devs.*
AccessOn.*
TopTechTidbits.*
DavidGoldfield.*
*.docx
tv_shows.md
science_playlist.md
silent_films.md
w3c-perspectives.md
Odyssey_Describer_Guide.md
*Wikipedia.htm
moveMisc.cmd
temp.*

# The context file for a particular film belongs to whoever wrote it; the ones
# in context/ are examples and ARE kept.
/video.md
/video-sequences.md

# ---- leftovers -------------------------------------------------------------
*.lockcheck
*_HomerScribe.exe
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
